cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sub-Ice, please cite the paper below (preferred citation) and the software version you used."
type: software
title: "Sub-Ice: Surface-based Ice Shelf Channel Extraction"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DylanKreynen/Sub-Ice"
abstract: >-
  Sub-Ice is a MATLAB algorithm for mapping ice shelf basal channels based on
  their surface expression in a digital elevation model (DEM). Given a DEM and
  start and end points for each channel of interest, Sub-Ice maps the channel
  centerline, extracts cross-sectional elevation profiles and delineates the
  channel edges. Channel width, depth and edge elevation are saved as tables,
  figures and georeferenced shapefiles.
keywords:
  - glaciology
  - ice shelves
  - basal channels
  - digital elevation model
  - MATLAB
